Our cloud cost anomaly monitor and SIEM paged on this burst of activity:
{"principal": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/stg-ci-deployer", "eventName": "RunInstances", "instanceType": "g5.4xlarge", "regions": ["ap-east-1", "eu-south-1", "sa-east-1"], "sourceIPAddress": "198.51.100.44"}
Our org only deploys workloads in `us-east-1`. What is the right investigation and containment workflow?

Triage this Kubernetes API audit entry from cluster k8s.lab.example:
{"verb":"list","user":{"username":"system:serviceaccount:staging:default"},"objectRef":{"resource":"secrets"},"sourceIPs":["10.10.42.19"],"responseStatus":{"code":200}}
What does this indicate and what should we check immediately?

Triage this cloud audit event:
{"eventName":"StopLogging","sourceIPAddress":"203.0.113.92","userIdentity":{"type":"AssumedRole","arn":"arn:aws:sts::000000000000:assumed-role/BreakGlassAdmin/temp-01"}}
Why is this an immediate high-severity signal and what should you investigate?

Before mirrored ingestion into registry.corp.example, an engineer flags this package.json diff in a transitive dependency:
"scripts": {
  "postinstall": "node ./scripts/telemetry-init.js --env"
}
What is the safest workflow to triage install-time hooks in npm or Python packages (setup.py) before approving them?

Multiple internal APIs trust tokens signed by sso.corp.example. During a penetration test, an access token minted for our low-impact feedback widget:
{"iss": "https://sso.corp.example", "sub": "usr_912", "aud": "https://feedback.corp.example", "scope": "read write"}
was accepted by https://payroll.corp.example because payroll only verified iss, exp, and signature. Explain this confused-deputy flaw and its fix.

Review this public-facing nginx server block for edge.corp.example:
server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    server_name edge.corp.example;
    ssl_protocols TLSv1 TLSv1.1 TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;
    client_max_body_size 0;
}
What configuration changes harden this reverse proxy against slow-read exhaustion, oversized payload abuse, banner leakage, and legacy TLS downgrades?
